# Capturing HTTP Login Form Data with Wireshark

## Overview

Wireshark is a network protocol analyzer that can capture and inspect network traffic. When a website uses **HTTP instead of HTTPS**, information submitted through an HTML form may be transmitted without encryption.

In this lab, we use the intentionally vulnerable **VULNWEB/Acunetix test website** to demonstrate how HTTP POST requests can be identified in Wireshark and how form data can be inspected.

> ⚠️ **Ethical and Legal Notice**
>
> Perform this experiment only on systems that you own or have explicit permission to test. The VULNWEB/Acunetix site is designed for security testing and learning. Do not capture credentials from other people's traffic or networks.

---

## Objective

The objectives of this lab are:

* Understand how HTTP login requests work.
* Capture HTTP traffic using Wireshark.
* Identify GET and POST requests.
* Locate an HTTP POST request containing HTML form data.
* Understand why HTTP is unsafe for transmitting login credentials.
* Observe the difference between HTTP and encrypted HTTPS traffic.

