# Step 9: 

The communication can be summarized as:

```text
Browser
   |
   | HTTP POST
   | Username + Password
   v
Web Server
```

Because HTTP does not encrypt the application data, someone who is authorized to observe that traffic can potentially inspect the contents of the HTTP request.

This is one of the major security problems with transmitting login information over plain HTTP.

---

# Step 10: Why HTTPS Is Important

HTTPS uses TLS encryption to protect HTTP communication.

With HTTPS, the communication is conceptually:

```text
Browser
   |
   | Encrypted HTTPS traffic
   | 🔒
   v
Web Server
```

Instead of directly seeing the submitted username and password in the captured HTTP request, a network observer normally sees encrypted TLS traffic.

Therefore:

```text
HTTP  → Data can be exposed
HTTPS → Data is encrypted in transit
```

